<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34391" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕlăgĭum</span></b> ,
			ii, v. pelagius, II. B.<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> † <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕlăgĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πελάγιος</span>, <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the sea</i>, <i>sea-</i> (pure Lat.
			marinus): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pelagii greges piscium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 3, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pelagiae conchae,</span>”
				<i>sea-mussels</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 29, 46, § 85</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cursus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 4, 20, 7</span></i>
			: matrona ornata phaleris pelagiis, i. e. <i>with
				pearls and corals</i>, P. Syrus ap.
				<i><span class="en">Petr. 55</span></i>— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕlăgĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>a kind of
				pearl-mussel</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 37, 61, §
			131</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕ-lăgĭum</span></b> ,
			ii, n., <i>purple color</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				9, 38, 62, § 134</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 40, 64, §
			138</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
